{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/394113-xp-freebies-for-old-player-new-character","id":394113,"title":"Xp/freebies for old player, new character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-05T14:27:05-08:00","id":394113,"title":"Xp/freebies for old player, new character","content":"What amount of xp/freebies do you think is fair to give if a player switched character mid chronicle.<br /> <br /> For example. I recently had a character retire because the goals of said character required him to travel away from the city and the remaining group decided to stay. So now a new character is needed and i'm wondering how much xp/freebies is fair to give the new character. Of course this is depending on concept etc.<br /> <br /> One option is to &quot;sell off&quot; all the traits invested in the character as freebies and give that amount to the new character.<br /> <br /> Another option is to not allow him any bonuses at all and just have basic character creation.<br /> <br /> Option 3 is somewhere in between.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:15:39-08:00","id":394163,"title":"","content":"If the character got written out of the story for reasons of good, natural roleplay, don't punish the player or they'll be less likely to play so naturally in the future even when it would hurt them. Think about what behavior you want to encourage or discourage. I guess if you really don't like seeing the group split up like that you can slap them for it and start their next character with nothing, but it kind of comes off as passive aggressive. Similarly if someone dies due to their player being a twit, there's no big need to throw xp at them because they earned that setback, but if they roleplay a heroic sacrifice, spotting their next character some xp will take the sting off of it and let people appreciate &quot;that was good drama&quot; instead of &quot;that sucks, now we have less ability as a group&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd say, give them some XP that approaches the rest of the group, as long as they don't cheese it. Hell you can even ask for the group's opinions, even the player in question: &quot;Thinking of assigning some extra XP to the next character to catch up, how much is fair? On par with everyone else, less, none?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T18:35:21-08:00","id":394342,"title":"","content":"Similar to what Traveller stated, I normally start the new character right around where the old character was if they died/left the group for roleplay reasons. If they died or left for stupid reasons, then the next character usually starts off at the lower end of wherever the group is XP-wise. I track how much XP each person gets over the course of the game, so it's easy enough to have the player build a new character with roughly the amount of the lowest other player (maybe a bit under, but not too much).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:22:43-08:00","id":394993,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't punish a player for bad play and reward another for good play in this situation. Good play usually nets more perks above and below the table in any case. If said player was making poor decisions, doing things that diminish other people's fun, etc. that player would probably be earning less XP in any case. (And you have a problem you have to deal with in ways other that trying to covertly condition the player by punishment for poor play during character replacement.) Likewise, a really good player has probably netted more XP and other perks (improved Backgrounds or just situational bonuses in the game.... e.g. more integration into the plots, NPC cast, etc.) .<br /> <br /> To that end, I would have a replacement character built the same as the initial character... Freebies for the base creation. Then add the XP purchases worth the total XP the previous character earned. If I was worried about twinkery, I might do something like having the new character forfeit unspent XP or allow them only to keep a certain amount (so the character isn't sitting there with a pile of XP to use for power-gaming purposes). I don't know what I'd do if the character used the rebuild as an opportunity for power-gaming, which is definitely a big possibility, except to say I have to okay the character build before it's cleared to come into the game. There is an inherent problem with giving players a character + a pile of XP. The character they build will usually be more optimized than the characters in the game that have developed organically.<br /> <br /> I would (and have) only imposed the &quot;you get the same XP as the lowest XP character in the group&quot; for completely new players. And then only if the characters are bunched together relatively closely. If you have massively different amounts of XP in the same group... there are more problems to deal with and I don't even begin to know the answer to that. (I've been a player who started a game, other players faded in and out and the solid core group didn't form until after my character had had several adventures. When the ST tried to equalize the situation, I understood intellectually, but viscerally, I was might pissed. I had earned each and every XP. They were just being handed them. And their builds were definitely more optimized than my character's, since he had been through several different party roles as the group kept morphing until settling down with the newer players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T10:17:06-08:00","id":395088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/394113-xp-freebies-for-old-player-new-character#post394113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What amount of xp/freebies do you think is fair to give if a player switched character mid chronicle.<br /> <br /> For example. I recently had a character retire because the goals of said character required him to travel away from the city and the remaining group decided to stay. So now a new character is needed and i'm wondering how much xp/freebies is fair to give the new character. Of course this is depending on concept etc.<br /> <br /> One option is to &quot;sell off&quot; all the traits invested in the character as freebies and give that amount to the new character.<br /> <br /> Another option is to not allow him any bonuses at all and just have basic character creation.<br /> <br /> Option 3 is somewhere in between.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. If this is a tabletop game with players expecting to be part of the same splatpack, then I would give him 90% of the XP of established characters to spend as he sees fit. OTOH, if this is a more sandboxy game or a LARP or something, I don't see much need to give him anything beyond my usual rewards for a detailed character history with plothooks and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}